{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"sequined-detectable-xanthareel","creation_channel":"cli","description":"S3 (2932) landed `bedrock_model_id` on LLMConfig (config.py:521), populated it from REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID / [tool.rebar.llm] bedrock_model_id (config.py:633-638), documented it in docs/env-vars.md:55, and duplicated its default literal in bedrock_model.py:38 with a hand-sync comment — but NOTHING READS IT. grep across src/ and tests/ finds no consumer besides the definition and the from_env assignment.\n\nEffect: an operator who sets REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID gets SILENCE — no model change, no warning, no error. The Bedrock model id is in fact carried by cfg.model as the `bedrock:<inference-profile-id>` string (providers.py parses provider from the prefix), so the documented knob is inert and misleading.\n\nFound while verifying the operator's per-pass model requirement for the cutover (see eb6e comment): this was the obvious candidate for a SECOND model knob that could express a per-pass mapping, and it turned out not to be wired at all.\n\nFix is a genuine choice, not a one-liner — either wire it (and define its precedence against the provider-prefixed cfg.model, which currently already carries the id) or delete it plus its docs entry and the duplicated literal. Should be decided alongside the per-pass config seam rather than in isolation, since that seam may want this field.","id":"281f-3336-c668-4979","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID is parsed and documented but read by nothing"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785435490210394001,"uuid":"1f0afc8a-41f7-48d1-a52c-b6840e8686ce"}